    <string name="meter_rules_title">How speed records work</string>
    <string name="meter_rules_subtitle">Tap to view the rules</string>
    <string name="meter_rules_line1">1. While you type, the meter shows your live characters per second (CPS).</string>
    <string name="meter_rules_line2">2. When you stop typing for the chosen window (5 sec / 10 sec / 1 min), the auto-swipe ends and the words you pressed in that window are counted.</string>
    <string name="meter_rules_line3">3. Every time you beat your best speed for a window, a record-break is saved with date &amp; time, word count, speed (CPS or CPM) and streak.</string>
    <string name="meter_rules_line4">4. Only record-breaking events appear in the list. Your streak grows while you keep beating your own record.</string>
    <string name="home_speed_title">Auto-Swipe Speed</string>
    <string name="home_speed_desc">The keyboard auto-measures every typing burst. When you pause for the chosen window (5 sec / 10 sec / 1 min), it stops and counts the words you pressed, computes CPS or CPM, then saves a record-break whenever you beat your best. The list and graph show only record-breaking entries, ordered by date &amp; time, per interval.</string>
